The FM engine in src/fm6/ is a TypeScript port of fm6_core.c from Felucca
(https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca, GPL-3.0-only, Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita,
Hügelton Instruments), which is itself an integer C port of msfa, the 6-operator FM core of Dexed:
  Copyright 2012 Google Inc., Copyright 2016-2025 Pascal Gauthier, licensed under Apache-2.0
  (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
Its lookup tables follow Felucca's tools/gen_tables.py and Felucca-Engines (MIT).

tests/fm6-gold.txt holds reference output produced by Felucca's fm6_core.c.

src/fm6/bank.ts: the WebSynth factory voices are original works of this project (GPL-3.0-only). They are written as
readable operator settings and were not copied from any instrument ROM.
src/fm6/factory.ts: the INIT voice and Felucca's 8 factory voices (GPL-3.0-only, Leo Kuroshita / Hügelton Instruments).

src/engines/: TypeScript ports of Felucca-Engines (https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca-Engines, MIT, Copyright (C) 2026
Leo Kuroshita, Hügelton Instruments): the shared DSP helpers and tables (dsp.c, gen_engine_tables.py), the ANALOG
engine and its host contract. tests/engines-golden.txt is that project's reference output (tests/golden.txt).

src/fx/: TypeScript ports of the effects of Felucca's fx.c (GPL-3.0-only): DIST, chorus, tempo delay, the ROOM,
SPRING and HALL reverbs and the master limiter. tests/fx-gold.txt is reference output of that code.
src/drum/: TypeScript ports of Felucca's drum_voice.c and the lane/kit logic of eng_drum.c (GPL-3.0-only).
tests/drum-gold.txt is reference output of drum_voice.c.

src/engines/formant.ts, src/engines/phys.ts: TypeScript ports of Felucca's eng_formant.c (VOICE, after Klatt 1980 and klattsch design
notes), eng_phys.c, phys_dsp.c and phys_symp.c (PHYS: DaisySP by Electrosmith / Emilie Gillet, MIT; Rings by Emilie Gillet, MIT; fixed-point ports
by Leo Kuroshita, GPL-3.0-only). tests/voice-gold.txt and tests/phys-gold.txt are reference output of that C code.

src/sampler/: TypeScript ports of Felucca's eng_sample.c, eng_grain.c and eng_slice.c (GPL-3.0-only) and their sample data
(tools/gen_samples.py output). The piano, flute and tenor sax sets are IMA ADPCM encodings of CC0 1.0 recordings by
Versilian Studios (Sam Gossner): VSCO-2 Community Edition (https://github.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE) and VCSL
(https://github.com/sgossner/VCSL). The drum break of SLICE is built from Felucca's generated drums (the Hügelton Sample
Pack, CC0 1.0). tests/sample-gold.txt, grain-gold.txt and slice-gold.txt are reference output of the C code.

src/fx/insert.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's INSERT effect (fx.c track_insert: SOFT, HARD, FOLD, FUZZ, CRUSH, PHASER, FLANGER, CHORUS; GPL-3.0-only).
src/fx/perform.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's performance layer (perform.c: REPEAT, REVERSE, LPF, HPF, TAPE STOP, FREEZE, OCT UP/DN, CRUSH, FLANGER, PHASER, REV/ECHO THROW, track mutes, the knob macros; GPL-3.0-only).
src/synth/voicelayer.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's voice allocation (voice.c: POLY / MONO / LEGATO / UNISON, priorities, glide, detune; GPL-3.0-only). SPREAD follows fx.c mix_spread.
src/synth/arp.ts, src/synth/chord.ts, src/synth/noteinput.ts: TypeScript ports of Felucca's arpeggiator (seq.c) and chord keys (chord.c; GPL-3.0-only).
src/seq/trackseq.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's step sequencer (seq.c: per-track length, division, swing and gate, ties, slides, ratchets, nudge, chances and conditions; GPL-3.0-only).
src/seq/motion.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's step automation and parameter locks (motion.c); the song sections follow song_chain.c (repeats, per-track lanes; GPL-3.0-only).
src/fx/slicer.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's SLICER insert (slicer.c: tempo-synced 16-step gate / stutter; GPL-3.0-only).
src/adpcm/dsp.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's adpcm_dsp.c, itself a C port of snes_spc 0.9.0 (SPC_DSP.cpp, Copyright (C) 2007 Shay Green; LGPL-2.1-or-later). src/adpcm/engine.ts, src/adpcm/data.ts: port of Felucca's eng_adpcm.c and its generated waves (tools/gen_adpcm.py; GPL-3.0-only).
src/sampler/user.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's user sample pipeline (tools/sampleio.py; GPL-3.0-only).
src/seq/midiclock.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's external MIDI clock follower (midi_clock.c, adapted there from contributions by ChanceTheMaker and keremimo; GPL-3.0-only). The MIDI channel controls and controller learn follow midi_control.c and midi_learn.c (adapted from a contribution by ChanceTheMaker).
src/mod/mod.ts: TypeScript port of Felucca's modulation matrix (mod.c) and track LFO (voice.c: waves, SYNC, FADE, S&H, SLEW; GPL-3.0-only).
tests/ins-gold.txt is reference output of that code.

src/drum/m808.ts, mlanes.ts, mkit.ts, mdsp.ts: TypeScript ports of Melodee's drum kits and DRUM engine (https://github.com/keremimo/melodee, GPL-3.0-only, Copyright (C) 2026 Kerem Kilic (Ellic Studio); retained Felucca portions Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita, Hügelton Instruments): KIT 808 (drum_808.c, after the TR-808 circuit studies of K. J. Werner et al., DAFx-14 and ICMC-SMC 2014), KIT CR78 (drum_cr78.c, designed after the CompuRhythm CR-78's voice list, not measured from a unit) and KIT FM (drum_fm.c) on the lanes of drum_lanes.c, and the kit, note, voice and MPC pad logic of eng_drum.c and voice.c; src/drum/fastmath.ts: x0x/fastmath.h.
src/drum/m909.ts: TypeScript port of Melodee's TR-909 kit (x0x/drum909.c, drum909_dsp.h, GPL-3.0-only, Modifications Copyright (C) 2026 Kerem Kilic). Melodee imported it from Charles Vestal's fm1-x0x (https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-x0x, commit 201e5c5c1ac056a028a006bd1eabb23ac1bb174d, GPL-3.0-only), which credits 9W9 by athousanddetails (GPL-3.0), derived from ER99 by Matthew Cieplak (GPL-3.0), for the 909 circuit models. The hats, crash and ride are Melodee's synthesized approximations, not a sample ROM; no sample or factory preset data is included. The tables are mathematical parameter curves and tanh values, generated as in Melodee's tools/gen_909_tables.py.
tests/melodee-drum-harness.c compiles Melodee's real sources (through its host simulator); tests/melodee-drum-gold.txt is reference output of that code. All of these files are GPL-3.0-only; none of the drum files carries another licence.
